{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NCuJzcfNVHjgy3EemWanhx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — entrainment_gated_ft\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n5\t- Backup: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n6\t- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n7\t\n8\t## Paper Type\n9\tEmpirical analysis paper (not method paper)\n10\t\n11\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n12\t\n13\t### Claim 1: Task-Specific Equalizer Effect\n14\tAdding attention layers to different linear recurrent architectures (GatedDeltaNet, RetNet, HGRN2) induces aggregate performance convergence whose strength scales with task retrieval demand—strongest on LAMBADA (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed, cross-arch std drops 79%), suggestive on ARC-Easy (ρ=-0.7, p=0.233 two-tailed, underpowered at n=5), absent on reasoning-heavy tasks (HellaSwag, WinoGrande). This continuous relationship between retrieval demand and convergence strength is a key finding, not a limitation of single-task significance.\n15\t\n16\t### Claim 2: Scale-Dependent Convergence\n17\tThe convergence effect is scale-dependent: monotonically complete at 1.3B parameters (Spearman ρ=-1.0 for cross-arch std vs attention ratio, exact permutation p=0.017, two-tailed) but only partial at 340M with a non-monotonic rebound at high attention ratios. Note: only two scale points available (Wang et al. do not provide 7B models); this is a binary contrast, not a multi-point trend. Paper must frame honestly as \"scale matters\" without implying extrapolation.\n18\t\n19\t### Claim 3: Architecture-Specific Effects (Equalizer Paradox)\n20\tDespite aggregate convergence, attention acts on almost entirely different sample subsets per architecture (pairwise Jaccard < 0.10). GDN and RetNet are hurt (net negative on LAMBADA), HGRN2 is helped (net positive), with symmetric effect magnitudes—convergence emerges from complementary, not redundant, effects. Surface-level features (token frequency, context length) do NOT differentiate helped vs hurt samples (all p>0.2 except marginal RetNet context_length). This rules out trivial explanations. Deeper features (perplexity under baseline, topic/domain) are being tested. If those also fail, claim wording shifts to \"architecture-specific effect whose mechanism is opaque to standard features\" — the non-overlapping Jaccard evidence remains hard regardless.\n21\t\n22\t## Story Spine\n23\t\n24\t### Problem\n25\tHybrid architectures mixing linear recurrence with full attention are becoming the dominant paradigm for efficient language models. A critical open question: does adding attention homogenize model behavior across different recurrence mechanisms, or do architecture-specific effects persist?\n26\t\n27\t### Existing Approaches & Gaps\n28\tWang et al. (2025, arXiv 2507.06457) provide the most comprehensive model zoo (72 models, 3 architectures, multiple scales and attention ratios) but report only aggregate metrics. They qualitatively note convergence trends but do not analyze: (a) the per-example mechanism, (b) scale dependency of convergence, (c) task-specificity, or (d) why architectures converge to similar *aggregate* performance through *different* individual-sample effects.\n29\t\n30\t### Our Framing\n31\tWe provide the first quantitative characterization of the \"equalizer effect\"—a systematic per-example analysis revealing that attention creates aggregate performance convergence through architecture-specific, largely non-overlapping mechanisms. This \"equalizer paradox\" (aggregate convergence + per-example divergence) has direct implications for architecture selection: even when aggregate metrics converge, the types of inputs each architecture handles well remain architecture-specific.\n32\t\n33\t### Headline Result Template\n34\t\"At 1.3B scale, adding attention layers reduces cross-architecture performance variance by 79% on LAMBADA (std 0.024→0.005), yet per-example analysis reveals the affected sample subsets are almost entirely non-overlapping across architectures (Jaccard < 0.10), with symmetric but opposite effect directions.\"\n35\t\n36\t## Venue Fit Risks\n37\t\n38\t### Risk 1: Architecture Analysis vs NLP\n39\tEMNLP is NLP-focused; this paper is closer to architecture analysis. **Mitigation**: Frame in terms of understanding language model behavior on specific linguistic tasks. Anchor analysis to token-level and context-level linguistic features (frequency, context length, retrieval demand). Include practical recommendations for practitioners choosing hybrid architectures for specific NLP tasks.\n40\t\n41\t### Risk 2: Limited Task Coverage\n42\tCurrently only LAMBADA shows clear convergence. **Mitigation**: (a) Extend per-example analysis to HellaSwag and other benchmarks, (b) provide principled explanation of LAMBADA's retrieval-dependent nature vs reasoning tasks, (c) if convergence appears on other retrieval tasks, strengthens Claim 1; if not, reframe as \"convergence is task-type-specific\" which is still interesting.\n43\t\n44\t### Risk 3: Small Architecture Sample\n45\tOnly 3 architectures (GDN, RetNet, HGRN2). **Mitigation**: These represent three distinct recurrence mechanisms (gated delta rule, linear attention with exponential decay, hierarchical gated recurrence). Check if Wang et al. have additional architectures or scales. n=3 is sufficient for the per-example analysis which is our main contribution.\n46\t\n47\t### Risk 4: Wang et al. Overlap\n48\tThey have the model zoo AND qualitative convergence observation. **Mitigation**: Our contribution is explicitly about what they did NOT do: quantitative convergence framework, scale-dependent analysis, per-example mechanism analysis. Frame as \"using their excellent model zoo, we discover a deeper phenomenon they missed.\"\n49\t\n50\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n51\t\n52\t### Concern A: \"This is just a negative result from a failed hypothesis\"\n53\tResponse: Frame as discovery paper. The equalizer effect is a positive finding—it was not the hypothesis we started with, but it's a genuine empirical phenomenon with theoretical implications. Many impactful papers come from unexpected findings.\n54\tRequired evidence: Strong standalone story; no mention of original entrainment hypothesis in the paper.\n55\t\n56\t### Concern B: \"Only one task shows the effect\" + Post-hoc taxonomy risk\n57\tResponse: Do NOT use binary retrieval/reasoning split — vulnerable to post-hoc cherry-picking (only 1 benchmark in \"retrieval\" category, exactly the one that's significant). Instead:\n58\t1. **Continuous spectrum**: Plot convergence strength (Spearman ρ) against a continuous measure of \"retrieval demand\" per benchmark. LAMBADA ρ=-1.0, ARC-E ρ=-0.7 (suggestive), ARC-C ρ=-0.3, HellaSwag/WinoGrande/MMLU near zero. Frame as dose-response: more retrieval demand → stronger convergence.\n59\t2. **Cite existing task taxonomies**: Use BIG-bench taxonomy or other published meta-analyses for task property classification — don't invent our own post-hoc.\n60\t3. **Honest reporting**: ARC-E ρ=-0.7 (p=0.117) is \"suggestive but underpowered\" — n=5 ratios means low statistical power. Continuous spectrum framing turns \"only LAMBADA significant\" into \"graded effect consistent with retrieval demand.\"\n61\t4. **Winogrande ambiguity**: Coreference resolution has a retrieval component (finding antecedent). Acknowledge this honestly rather than forcing it into \"reasoning.\"\n62\t5. **exp-002 validation**: If HellaSwag per-example analysis confirms no convergence at sample level, upgrades from \"aggregate not significant\" to \"per-example confirmed non-converging.\"\n63\tRequired experiments: exp-001 (done, PASS on dichotomy), exp-002 (per-example validation), exp-003 (sample characterization).\n64\t\n65\t### Concern C: \"No causal mechanism\"\n66\tResponse: Per-example analysis provides mechanistic evidence (different subsets). Strengthen with attention weight visualization and sample feature characterization.\n67\tRequired experiments: Sample characterization (exp-003), attention weight analysis (exp-004).\n68\t\n69\t### Concern D: \"n=3 architectures is too few\"\n70\tResponse: Three architectures with 5 attention ratios × 2 scales = 30 models. The per-example analysis provides thousands of data points. Check if additional architectures available.\n71\tRequired experiments: Architecture expansion check (exp-005).\n72\t\n73\t### Concern E: \"Two scales don't establish a trend\"\n74\tResponse: 7B unavailable (Wang et al. capped at 1.3B). Frame as \"binary contrast showing scale is a necessary condition\" — convergence requires sufficient model capacity (1.3B), not just attention. Strengthen via exp-007 (340M rebound mechanism analysis) to provide mechanistic explanation for the scale gap. Acknowledge as limitation; do not imply extrapolation.\n75\tRequired experiments: exp-007 (340M rebound mechanism).\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7ff5ff9-a534-4909-96dd-e2798498e0e9","uuid":"9c73183a-dbf1-411c-9e45-4d0f4b449ada","timestamp":"2026-05-19T14:08:07.978Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T135121/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — entrainment_gated_ft\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Backup: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n\n## Paper Type\nEmpirical analysis paper (not method paper)\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n### Claim 1: Task-Specific Equalizer Effect\nAdding attention layers to different linear recurrent architectures (GatedDeltaNet, RetNet, HGRN2) induces aggregate performance convergence whose strength scales with task retrieval demand—strongest on LAMBADA (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed, cross-arch std drops 79%), suggestive on ARC-Easy (ρ=-0.7, p=0.233 two-tailed, underpowered at n=5), absent on reasoning-heavy tasks (HellaSwag, WinoGrande). This continuous relationship between retrieval demand and convergence strength is a key finding, not a limitation of single-task significance.\n\n### Claim 2: Scale-Dependent Convergence\nThe convergence effect is scale-dependent: monotonically complete at 1.3B parameters (Spearman ρ=-1.0 for cross-arch std vs attention ratio, exact permutation p=0.017, two-tailed) but only partial at 340M with a non-monotonic rebound at high attention ratios. Note: only two scale points available (Wang et al. do not provide 7B models); this is a binary contrast, not a multi-point trend. Paper must frame honestly as \"scale matters\" without implying extrapolation.\n\n### Claim 3: Architecture-Specific Effects (Equalizer Paradox)\nDespite aggregate convergence, attention acts on almost entirely different sample subsets per architecture (pairwise Jaccard < 0.10). GDN and RetNet are hurt (net negative on LAMBADA), HGRN2 is helped (net positive), with symmetric effect magnitudes—convergence emerges from complementary, not redundant, effects. Surface-level features (token frequency, context length) do NOT differentiate helped vs hurt samples (all p>0.2 except marginal RetNet context_length). This rules out trivial explanations. Deeper features (perplexity under baseline, topic/domain) are being tested. If those also fail, claim wording shifts to \"architecture-specific effect whose mechanism is opaque to standard features\" — the non-overlapping Jaccard evidence remains hard regardless.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nHybrid architectures mixing linear recurrence with full attention are becoming the dominant paradigm for efficient language models. A critical open question: does adding attention homogenize model behavior across different recurrence mechanisms, or do architecture-specific effects persist?\n\n### Existing Approaches & Gaps\nWang et al. (2025, arXiv 2507.06457) provide the most comprehensive model zoo (72 models, 3 architectures, multiple scales and attention ratios) but report only aggregate metrics. They qualitatively note convergence trends but do not analyze: (a) the per-example mechanism, (b) scale dependency of convergence, (c) task-specificity, or (d) why architectures converge to similar *aggregate* performance through *different* individual-sample effects.\n\n### Our Framing\nWe provide the first quantitative characterization of the \"equalizer effect\"—a systematic per-example analysis revealing that attention creates aggregate performance convergence through architecture-specific, largely non-overlapping mechanisms. This \"equalizer paradox\" (aggregate convergence + per-example divergence) has direct implications for architecture selection: even when aggregate metrics converge, the types of inputs each architecture handles well remain architecture-specific.\n\n### Headline Result Template\n\"At 1.3B scale, adding attention layers reduces cross-architecture performance variance by 79% on LAMBADA (std 0.024→0.005), yet per-example analysis reveals the affected sample subsets are almost entirely non-overlapping across architectures (Jaccard < 0.10), with symmetric but opposite effect directions.\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n### Risk 1: Architecture Analysis vs NLP\nEMNLP is NLP-focused; this paper is closer to architecture analysis. **Mitigation**: Frame in terms of understanding language model behavior on specific linguistic tasks. Anchor analysis to token-level and context-level linguistic features (frequency, context length, retrieval demand). Include practical recommendations for practitioners choosing hybrid architectures for specific NLP tasks.\n\n### Risk 2: Limited Task Coverage\nCurrently only LAMBADA shows clear convergence. **Mitigation**: (a) Extend per-example analysis to HellaSwag and other benchmarks, (b) provide principled explanation of LAMBADA's retrieval-dependent nature vs reasoning tasks, (c) if convergence appears on other retrieval tasks, strengthens Claim 1; if not, reframe as \"convergence is task-type-specific\" which is still interesting.\n\n### Risk 3: Small Architecture Sample\nOnly 3 architectures (GDN, RetNet, HGRN2). **Mitigation**: These represent three distinct recurrence mechanisms (gated delta rule, linear attention with exponential decay, hierarchical gated recurrence). Check if Wang et al. have additional architectures or scales. n=3 is sufficient for the per-example analysis which is our main contribution.\n\n### Risk 4: Wang et al. Overlap\nThey have the model zoo AND qualitative convergence observation. **Mitigation**: Our contribution is explicitly about what they did NOT do: quantitative convergence framework, scale-dependent analysis, per-example mechanism analysis. Frame as \"using their excellent model zoo, we discover a deeper phenomenon they missed.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### Concern A: \"This is just a negative result from a failed hypothesis\"\nResponse: Frame as discovery paper. The equalizer effect is a positive finding—it was not the hypothesis we started with, but it's a genuine empirical phenomenon with theoretical implications. Many impactful papers come from unexpected findings.\nRequired evidence: Strong standalone story; no mention of original entrainment hypothesis in the paper.\n\n### Concern B: \"Only one task shows the effect\" + Post-hoc taxonomy risk\nResponse: Do NOT use binary retrieval/reasoning split — vulnerable to post-hoc cherry-picking (only 1 benchmark in \"retrieval\" category, exactly the one that's significant). Instead:\n1. **Continuous spectrum**: Plot convergence strength (Spearman ρ) against a continuous measure of \"retrieval demand\" per benchmark. LAMBADA ρ=-1.0, ARC-E ρ=-0.7 (suggestive), ARC-C ρ=-0.3, HellaSwag/WinoGrande/MMLU near zero. Frame as dose-response: more retrieval demand → stronger convergence.\n2. **Cite existing task taxonomies**: Use BIG-bench taxonomy or other published meta-analyses for task property classification — don't invent our own post-hoc.\n3. **Honest reporting**: ARC-E ρ=-0.7 (p=0.117) is \"suggestive but underpowered\" — n=5 ratios means low statistical power. Continuous spectrum framing turns \"only LAMBADA significant\" into \"graded effect consistent with retrieval demand.\"\n4. **Winogrande ambiguity**: Coreference resolution has a retrieval component (finding antecedent). Acknowledge this honestly rather than forcing it into \"reasoning.\"\n5. **exp-002 validation**: If HellaSwag per-example analysis confirms no convergence at sample level, upgrades from \"aggregate not significant\" to \"per-example confirmed non-converging.\"\nRequired experiments: exp-001 (done, PASS on dichotomy), exp-002 (per-example validation), exp-003 (sample characterization).\n\n### Concern C: \"No causal mechanism\"\nResponse: Per-example analysis provides mechanistic evidence (different subsets). Strengthen with attention weight visualization and sample feature characterization.\nRequired experiments: Sample characterization (exp-003), attention weight analysis (exp-004).\n\n### Concern D: \"n=3 architectures is too few\"\nResponse: Three architectures with 5 attention ratios × 2 scales = 30 models. The per-example analysis provides thousands of data points. Check if additional architectures available.\nRequired experiments: Architecture expansion check (exp-005).\n\n### Concern E: \"Two scales don't establish a trend\"\nResponse: 7B unavailable (Wang et al. capped at 1.3B). Frame as \"binary contrast showing scale is a necessary condition\" — convergence requires sufficient model capacity (1.3B), not just attention. Strengthen via exp-007 (340M rebound mechanism analysis) to provide mechanistic explanation for the scale gap. Acknowledge as limitation; do not imply extrapolation.\nRequired experiments: exp-007 (340M rebound mechanism).\n","numLines":76,"startLine":1,"totalLines":76}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RNfedeNffKGKy5LZAumzSX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis (task-specificity validation)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Re-run lm-eval with --log_samples on 1.3B models (GDN, RetNet, HGRN2 at h0/h3-1/h6-1/h12-1/h24-1) for HellaSwag, ARC-Easy, ARC-Challenge. Also collect 340M RetNet+HGRN2 (10 models) and 1.3B GDN h3-1/h6-1/h24-1 missing configs. Compute per-example helped/hurt sets, pairwise Jaccard, and per-example convergence metrics analogous to LAMBADA analysis.\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"hellaswag_per_example_convergence\": false,\n7\t      \"hellaswag_jaccard_cross_arch_mean\": 0.18,\n8\t      \"hellaswag_jaccard_interpretation\": \"near-random overlap, no systematic pattern\",\n9\t      \"hellaswag_helped_hurt_net_direction\": \"inconsistent across architectures and attention ratios\",\n10\t      \"arc_easy_per_example_convergence\": \"noisy/suggestive\",\n11\t      \"arc_easy_jaccard_cross_arch_mean\": 0.12,\n12\t      \"arc_easy_std_reduction_pct\": 38,\n13\t      \"arc_easy_std_reduction_p\": 0.14,\n14\t      \"arc_easy_helped_hurt_asymmetry\": \"present but unstable across attention ratios\",\n15\t      \"arc_challenge_per_example_convergence\": false,\n16\t      \"arc_challenge_jaccard_cross_arch_mean\": 0.15,\n17\t      \"arc_challenge_std_reduction_pct\": 12,\n18\t      \"dose_response_rho_6benchmarks\": -0.66,\n19\t      \"dose_response_rho_p\": 0.16,\n20\t      \"n_benchmarks_per_example_confirmed_converging\": 1,\n21\t      \"n_benchmarks_suggestive\": 1,\n22\t      \"n_benchmarks_confirmed_non_converging\": 4,\n23\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 18\n24\t    },\n25\t    \"tables\": [\n26\t      {\n27\t        \"title\": \"Table: Per-example convergence metrics across benchmarks (1.3B)\",\n28\t        \"columns\": [\n29\t          \"Benchmark\",\n30\t          \"Retrieval Demand\",\n31\t          \"Aggregate ρ (std vs attn)\",\n32\t          \"Aggregate p\",\n33\t          \"Per-example Jaccard (mean pairwise)\",\n34\t          \"Std Reduction %\",\n35\t          \"Per-example Verdict\"\n36\t        ],\n37\t        \"rows\": [\n38\t          [\n39\t            \"LAMBADA\",\n40\t            \"High\",\n41\t            -1.0,\n42\t            0.008,\n43\t            0.08,\n44\t            \"79%\",\n45\t            \"Converging (architecture-specific mechanism)\"\n46\t          ],\n47\t          [\n48\t            \"ARC-Easy\",\n49\t            \"Medium\",\n50\t            -0.7,\n51\t            0.117,\n52\t            0.12,\n53\t            \"38%\",\n54\t            \"Noisy/suggestive\"\n55\t          ],\n56\t          [\n57\t            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n58\t            \"Low-Medium\",\n59\t            -0.3,\n60\t            0.624,\n61\t            0.15,\n62\t            \"12%\",\n63\t            \"Non-converging\"\n64\t          ],\n65\t          [\n66\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n67\t            \"Low\",\n68\t            0.3,\n69\t            0.742,\n70\t            0.18,\n71\t            \"-5%\",\n72\t            \"Non-converging (confirmed per-example)\"\n73\t          ],\n74\t          [\n75\t            \"WinoGrande\",\n76\t            \"Low*\",\n77\t            0.1,\n78\t            0.608,\n79\t            \"N/A†\",\n80\t            \"3%\",\n81\t            \"Non-converging\"\n82\t          ],\n83\t          [\n84\t            \"MMLU\",\n85\t            \"Mixed\",\n86\t            -0.7,\n87\t            0.117,\n88\t            \"N/A†\",\n89\t            \"22%\",\n90\t            \"Unclear (aggregate suggestive, no per-example data)\"\n91\t          ]\n92\t        ],\n93\t        \"notes\": \"†Per-example data not collected for WinoGrande/MMLU in this experiment. *WinoGrande has coreference retrieval component; acknowledged in text.\"\n94\t      }\n95\t    ],\n96\t    \"figures\": [],\n97\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-002 的 median 结果确认 task-specificity 是真实的，但把 \\\"dose-response\\\" 的统计力量限制在了 descriptive level。论文的关键修辞策略：不要声称 dose-response 是 \\\"established\\\"，而是用 \\\"consistent with a retrieval-demand gradient\\\" + \\\"preliminary due to limited benchmark-level n\\\" 的措辞。 HellaSwag per-example 确认非收敛这一点很有价值——把 aggregate p=0.742 升级为 \\\"per-example confirmed non-converging\\\"，排除了 \\\"aggregate 不显著只是因为 power 不够\\\" 的可能性。 ARC-E 的 noisy 结果实际上对叙事有利：它不是 retrieval 纯任务，所以 partial/noisy convergence 正好符合 \\\"retrieval demand 越高收敛越强\\\" 的 gradient story。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档下，equalizer effect 本质上是 retrieval-gated 的。LAMBADA 是纯粹的 last-word retrieval 任务， attention 机制对此类任务有直接的结构性优势（回看上下文定位 target word），因此 per-example 收敛清晰。 ARC-Easy 包含部分 retrieval 成分（从选项中匹配已知事实），但混合了推理成分，导致 per-example 层面噪声大—— Jaccard 结构模糊，helped/hurt 集合随 attention ratio 变化不稳定，aggregate std 降低存在但不显著。 HellaSwag 和 ARC-Challenge 主要依赖 commonsense reasoning 和 multi-step inference，attention 的贡献 分散在多种推理路径上而非集中在 retrieval 上，因此 per-example 分析确认了 aggregate 层面的非收敛： 不同架构被 attention 帮助/伤害的样本几乎是随机的，无系统性结构。 这使 dose-response 本质上变成了 2-point gradient：LAMBADA 强，ARC-E suggestive，其余 flat。 6 个 benchmark 的 Spearman ρ≈-0.66（在 [-0.75, -0.55] 范围内）但因 n=6 且非线性分布，p≈0.16 不显著—— 这足以支持 \\\"retrieval demand 调节收敛强度\\\" 的叙事，但必须承认是 preliminary observation 而非 established relationship。\\n\"\n98\t  },\n99\t  {\n100\t    \"name\": \"Helped/hurt sample characterization Phase 2 (perplexity + topic/domain)\",\n101\t    \"description\": \"在 Phase 1 surface features 全部 non-significant 的基础上，Phase 2 测试更深层特征： (a) 各架构 pure recurrent baseline (h0) 下每个 LAMBADA 样本的 perplexity， (b) 基于 LAMBADA 文本内容的 topic/domain 分布 (LDA 或预训练 topic model)。 检验 helped/hurt 样本是否在这些特征上可区分。\\n\",\n102\t    \"results\": {\n103\t      \"perplexity_gdn_helped_vs_hurt_p\": 0.031,\n104\t      \"perplexity_gdn_helped_vs_hurt_cohens_d\": 0.19,\n105\t      \"perplexity_gdn_direction\": \"hurt samples have higher baseline perplexity (harder under pure recurrence)\",\n106\t      \"perplexity_hgrn2_helped_vs_hurt_p\": 0.22,\n107\t      \"perplexity_hgrn2_helped_vs_hurt_cohens_d\": 0.08,\n108\t      \"perplexity_retnet_helped_vs_hurt_p\": 0.09,\n109\t      \"perplexity_retnet_helped_vs_hurt_cohens_d\": 0.13,\n110\t      \"topic_gdn_chi2_p\": 0.34,\n111\t      \"topic_hgrn2_chi2_p\": 0.51,\n112\t      \"topic_retnet_chi2_p\": 0.28,\n113\t      \"cross_arch_perplexity_interaction_p\": 0.07,\n114\t      \"n_features_significant_any_arch\": 1,\n115\t      \"n_features_significant_cross_arch\": 0,\n116\t      \"overall_mechanism_status\": \"opaque to tested features; perplexity suggestive for GDN only\"\n117\t    },\n118\t    \"tables\": [\n119\t      {\n120\t        \"title\": \"Table: Phase 2 feature analysis — helped vs hurt sample characterization\",\n121\t        \"columns\": [\n122\t          \"Feature\",\n123\t          \"Architecture\",\n124\t          \"Test\",\n125\t          \"p-value\",\n126\t          \"Effect Size (d/V)\",\n127\t          \"Direction\",\n128\t          \"Significant?\"\n129\t        ],\n130\t        \"rows\": [\n131\t          [\n132\t            \"Baseline perplexity (h0)\",\n133\t            \"GDN\",\n134\t            \"Mann-Whitney U\",\n135\t            0.031,\n136\t            \"d=0.19\",\n137\t            \"Hurt > Helped\",\n138\t            \"Marginal*\"\n139\t          ],\n140\t          [\n141\t            \"Baseline perplexity (h0)\",\n142\t            \"HGRN2\",\n143\t            \"Mann-Whitney U\",\n144\t            0.22,\n145\t            \"d=0.08\",\n146\t            \"—\",\n147\t            \"No\"\n148\t          ],\n149\t          [\n150\t            \"Baseline perplexity (h0)\",\n151\t            \"RetNet\",\n152\t            \"Mann-Whitney U\",\n153\t            0.09,\n154\t            \"d=0.13\",\n155\t            \"Hurt > Helped (trend)\",\n156\t            \"No\"\n157\t          ],\n158\t          [\n159\t            \"Topic distribution\",\n160\t            \"GDN\",\n161\t            \"Chi-squared\",\n162\t            0.34,\n163\t            \"V=0.06\",\n164\t            \"—\",\n165\t            \"No\"\n166\t          ],\n167\t          [\n168\t            \"Topic distribution\",\n169\t            \"HGRN2\",\n170\t            \"Chi-squared\",\n171\t            0.51,\n172\t            \"V=0.04\",\n173\t            \"—\",\n174\t            \"No\"\n175\t          ],\n176\t          [\n177\t            \"Topic distribution\",\n178\t            \"RetNet\",\n179\t            \"Chi-squared\",\n180\t            0.28,\n181\t            \"V=0.07\",\n182\t            \"—\",\n183\t            \"No\"\n184\t          ],\n185\t          [\n186\t            \"Perplexity × Arch interaction\",\n187\t            \"All\",\n188\t            \"Two-way ANOVA\",\n189\t            0.07,\n190\t            \"η²=0.003\",\n191\t            \"—\",\n192\t            \"No (trend)\"\n193\t          ]\n194\t        ],\n195\t        \"notes\": \"*Marginal: 0.01 < p < 0.05, below preregistered p<0.01 threshold for individual tests. After Bonferroni correction (6 tests), adjusted p=0.186.\"\n196\t      }\n197\t    ],\n198\t    \"figures\": [],\n199\t    \"analysis\": \"Phase 2 的 GDN perplexity signal (p=0.031) 在论文中的定位需要谨慎：它通过了 nominal 0.05 但 未通过 preregistered 0.01，且 Bonferroni 校正后不显著。论文应报告为 \\\"suggestive lead for future work\\\"， 不作为 claimed finding。关键叙事价值在负面结果的累积：surface features (Phase 1) + perplexity + topic 全部失败或 marginal，系统性地排除了从简单到中等复杂度的解释，让 \\\"mechanism is opaque\\\" 不是一句空话 而是有实证支撑的 negative characterization。这对 EMNLP Findings 审稿人来说是可接受的—— 他们会 appreciate careful negative results over overclaimed positive ones。\\n\\n\\nmedian 档的核心假设是 mechanism 保持 opaque。Phase 2 的 perplexity 特征比 surface features 更有信息量， 因为它直接衡量 \\\"pure recurrence 下的困难度\\\"——直觉上，attention 最可能帮助那些 recurrence 本身处理不好的样本。 但这个直觉只在一个架构 (GDN) 上得到 marginal 验证 (p=0.031, d=0.19)：GDN 的 gated delta rule 机制 在高 perplexity 样本上可能有特定的弱点（例如需要精确的长距离 copy 但 delta rule 的 memory update 不够精确），attention 填补了这个缺口。HGRN2 和 RetNet 的 hierarchical/exponential decay 机制 处理困难样本的方式不同，perplexity 不是它们的瓶颈维度，所以信号消失。 Topic/domain 特征完全 non-significant：attention 的效果不是 \\\"对某些 domain 更有用\\\"， 而是在每个 domain 内部都有 architecture-specific 的帮助/伤害模式。 这实际上强化了 \\\"opaque mechanism\\\" 的叙事——连中间层特征 (perplexity) 也只给出了微弱线索， 说明 equalizer effect 的机制深嵌在 recurrence-attention 交互的计算层面。\\n\"\n200\t  },\n201\t  {\n202\t    \"name\": \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\",\n203\t    \"description\": \"提取 3 个架构 h3-1 配置的 attention weight patterns (1.3B)。 在 LAMBADA 样本上计算：(a) attention 聚焦位置分布，(b) attention pattern 与 helped/hurt 身份的相关性， (c) 跨架构 attention pattern 相似度。\\n\",\n204\t    \"results\": {\n205\t      \"gdn_attention_entropy_mean\": 3.2,\n206\t      \"hgrn2_attention_entropy_mean\": 2.8,\n207\t      \"retnet_attention_entropy_mean\": 3.0,\n208\t      \"attention_focus_on_target_context_pct_gdn\": 0.42,\n209\t      \"attention_focus_on_target_context_pct_hgrn2\": 0.58,\n210\t      \"attention_focus_on_target_context_pct_retnet\": 0.47,\n211\t      \"cross_arch_attention_cosine_similarity_mean\": 0.35,\n212\t      \"attention_pattern_correlation_with_helped_gdn\": 0.18,\n213\t      \"attention_pattern_correlation_with_helped_hgrn2\": 0.27,\n214\t      \"attention_pattern_correlation_with_helped_retnet\": 0.22,\n215\t      \"attention_pattern_correlation_mean\": 0.22,\n216\t      \"passes_preregistered_threshold\": false,\n217\t      \"qualitative_patterns_visible\": true,\n218\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 3.5\n219\t    },\n220\t    \"tables\": [\n221\t      {\n222\t        \"title\": \"Table: Attention pattern analysis summary (h3-1 config, 1.3B)\",\n223\t        \"columns\": [\n224\t          \"Architecture\",\n225\t          \"Attn Entropy (mean)\",\n226\t          \"Target Context Focus %\",\n227\t          \"Corr with Helped/Hurt (r)\",\n228\t          \"Corr p-value\"\n229\t        ],\n230\t        \"rows\": [\n231\t          [\n232\t            \"GDN\",\n233\t            3.2,\n234\t            \"42%\",\n235\t            0.18,\n236\t            0.002\n237\t          ],\n238\t          [\n239\t            \"HGRN2\",\n240\t            2.8,\n241\t            \"58%\",\n242\t            0.27,\n243\t            \"<0.001\"\n244\t          ],\n245\t          [\n246\t            \"RetNet\",\n247\t            3.0,\n248\t            \"47%\",\n249\t            0.22,\n250\t            \"<0.001\"\n251\t          ]\n252\t        ],\n253\t        \"notes\": \"All correlations significant due to large n (>900 samples) but effect sizes below preregistered r>0.3 threshold. Target Context Focus = fraction of attention weight on tokens within 10-token window preceding target word.\"\n254\t      },\n255\t      {\n256\t        \"title\": \"Table: Cross-architecture attention pattern similarity\",\n257\t        \"columns\": [\n258\t          \"Architecture Pair\",\n259\t          \"Cosine Similarity (mean)\",\n260\t          \"Similarity on Helped Samples\",\n261\t          \"Similarity on Hurt Samples\"\n262\t        ],\n263\t        \"rows\": [\n264\t          [\n265\t            \"GDN–HGRN2\",\n266\t            0.31,\n267\t            0.28,\n268\t            0.33\n269\t          ],\n270\t          [\n271\t            \"GDN–RetNet\",\n272\t            0.38,\n273\t            0.35,\n274\t            0.4\n275\t          ],\n276\t          [\n277\t            \"HGRN2–RetNet\",\n278\t            0.36,\n279\t            0.32,\n280\t            0.39\n281\t          ]\n282\t        ],\n283\t        \"notes\": \"Similarity computed on attention weight vectors averaged over heads and layers. Low similarity consistent with architecture-specific attention usage.\"\n284\t      }\n285\t    ],\n286\t    \"figures\": [],\n287\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-004 的 median 结果产出两类价值：(1) 定性 illustration 素材（attention heatmap triptych 将成为论文最直观的 figure，直接展示 \\\"same input, different attention patterns\\\" 的 paradox）， (2) 进一步的 negative quantitative evidence 强化 \\\"opaque mechanism\\\" 叙事。 关键措辞：attention pattern 与 helped/hurt 有 \\\"detectable but weak association\\\" (r≈0.22)， 说明 attention 的作用不完全随机，但远不足以 predict 或 explain 哪些样本被帮助/伤害。 这与 Phase 2 perplexity 的 marginal signal 形成呼应——mechanism 有线索但不可解。 审稿人 Concern C (\\\"No causal mechanism\\\") 的回应变为：\\\"We provide three levels of mechanistic evidence — all suggestive, none conclusive — establishing the phenomenon's depth.\\\"\\n\\n\\nmedian 档预测 attention correlation r=0.15–0.30，低于 preregistered r>0.3 threshold。 原因在于 attention 的作用路径是间接的：attention layer 不仅直接影响输出 logits， 还通过修改 hidden state 影响后续 recurrent layers 的计算。因此 attention weight pattern 本身只捕获了 \\\"attention 在看什么\\\" 而非 \\\"attention 如何改变了下游计算\\\"。 具体来说：HGRN2 的 hierarchical gating 与 attention 有最强的协同 (r=0.27)，因为 HGRN2 的层级结构天然需要不同粒度的信息，attention 提供的全局视野与其互补性最强；GDN 的 delta rule 更新机制与 attention 的交互更复杂 (r=0.18)，因为 delta rule 的精确 memory 操作可能 在某些层 override attention 的影响。 定性上，attention heatmap 会显示有趣的模式：例如 HGRN2 的 attention 更集中在 sentence boundaries 和 target-word context windows，而 GDN 的 attention 更分散——但这些差异在统计检验中被 样本间噪声淹没。论文中作为 qualitative illustration 展示，配合 \\\"future work: causal intervention on attention weights\\\" 的讨论。\\n\"\n288\t  },\n289\t  {\n290\t    \"name\": \"Architecture expansion check\",\n291\t    \"description\": \"搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 及公开 repos (HuggingFace, GitHub) 寻找额外的 hybrid 架构 (Mamba/Mamba2 hybrid, RWKV hybrid, Griffin, etc.)。如果找到，在 LAMBADA 上评估收敛模式。\\n\",\n292\t    \"results\": {\n293\t      \"additional_architectures_found\": 0,\n294\t      \"mamba_hybrid_status\": \"no Wang et al. equivalent; community checkpoints exist but different training setup (not comparable)\",\n295\t      \"rwkv_hybrid_status\": \"RWKV-6 hybrid mentioned in literature but no public 1.3B checkpoint with matched attention ratios\",\n296\t      \"griffin_status\": \"Google proprietary, no public weights\",\n297\t      \"search_exhaustive\": true,\n298\t      \"n_architectures_final\": 3,\n299\t      \"mitigation_framing\": \"3 architectures represent 3 distinct recurrence mechanisms (gated delta rule, linear attention + exp decay, hierarchical gated recurrence); acknowledged as limitation\"\n300\t    },\n301\t    \"tables\": [],\n302\t    \"figures\": [],\n303\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-005 的 null result 对论文的影响是 Limitations 段必须明确写 \\\"n=3 architectures\\\" 并 呼吁社区建立更大的 standardized hybrid model zoo。这是审稿人 Concern D 的直接回应。 在 median 档下，审稿人可能把这作为 \\\"not Main, push to Findings\\\" 的理由之一， 但不太可能因此 reject——因为 per-example analysis 的 novelty 不依赖架构数量。\\n\\n\\nmedian 档假设找不到额外可比架构。Wang et al. 的 model zoo 是目前最全面的 hybrid 架构实验—— 他们选择 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 正是因为这三个有公开实现且代表了三大类 recurrence 机制。 Mamba hybrid (Jamba) 由 AI21 发布但训练 setup 完全不同（不同数据、不同 tokenizer、不同规模点）， 不能直接加入 controlled comparison。RWKV hybrid 讨论较多但标准化的 attention ratio sweep checkpoint 不存在。Griffin 是 Google 的 proprietary architecture。 n=3 在 median 档下必须诚实承认为 limitation，但论文可以辩护：per-example analysis 提供了 上千个 data points，三个架构覆盖了三种根本不同的 recurrence 机制，且 convergence 效应在 所有三个上都观测到——这不是 \\\"cherry-picked 一个能 work 的架构\\\"。\\n\"\n304\t  },\n305\t  {\n306\t    \"name\": \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\",\n307\t    \"description\": \"深入分析 340M 在 attn=8 处的非单调 rebound。与 1.3B 同 attention ratio 进行 per-example 比较， 识别 diverging samples。分析 training token count (20B vs 100B) 作为 confound。\\n\",\n308\t    \"results\": {\n309\t      \"rebound_samples_overlap_with_hardest_pct\": 62,\n310\t      \"rebound_samples_overlap_with_hardest_ci95\": [\n311\t        48,\n312\t        74\n313\t      ],\n314\t      \"hardest_definition\": \"bottom 20% accuracy under 340M h0 baseline\",\n315\t      \"rebound_at_1_3b_same_ratio\": \"no rebound (monotonic convergence continues)\",\n316\t      \"scale_delta_explanation_pct\": 45,\n317\t      \"scale_delta_explanation\": \"340M rebound partially explained by capacity saturation on hard samples\",\n318\t      \"training_token_confound_disentangled\": false,\n319\t      \"training_token_analysis\": \"340M trained on 20B tokens, 1.3B on 100B tokens; rebound samples have higher perplexity under both scales but magnitude differs; cannot separate scale vs data effects\",\n320\t      \"confound_correlation_with_rebound\": 0.31,\n321\t      \"mechanism_confidence\": \"partial — capacity explanation plausible but token confound unresolved\",\n322\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 1.5\n323\t    },\n324\t    \"tables\": [\n325\t      {\n326\t        \"title\": \"Table: 340M rebound analysis — sample characterization\",\n327\t        \"columns\": [\n328\t          \"Sample Group\",\n329\t          \"N\",\n330\t          \"340M h0 Acc\",\n331\t          \"340M h8 Acc\",\n332\t          \"1.3B h0 Acc\",\n333\t          \"1.3B h8 Acc\",\n334\t          \"Rebound?\"\n335\t        ],\n336\t        \"rows\": [\n337\t          [\n338\t            \"Rebound samples (340M)\",\n339\t            187,\n340\t            \"31%\",\n341\t            \"28%\",\n342\t            \"52%\",\n343\t            \"61%\",\n344\t            \"Yes at 340M, No at 1.3B\"\n345\t          ],\n346\t          [\n347\t            \"Non-rebound samples (340M)\",\n348\t            4926,\n349\t            \"78%\",\n350\t            \"82%\",\n351\t            \"85%\",\n352\t            \"89%\",\n353\t            \"No\"\n354\t          ],\n355\t          [\n356\t            \"Overlap with hardest 20%\",\n357\t            \"116/187 (62%)\",\n358\t            \"—\",\n359\t            \"—\",\n360\t            \"—\",\n361\t            \"—\",\n362\t            \"—\"\n363\t          ]\n364\t        ],\n365\t        \"notes\": \"Rebound samples defined as those with accuracy drop from h6 to h8 at 340M. Hardest 20% = bottom quintile of h0 accuracy.\"\n366\t      },\n367\t      {\n368\t        \"title\": \"Table: Training token confound assessment\",\n369\t        \"columns\": [\n370\t          \"Factor\",\n371\t          \"Correlation with Rebound Magnitude\",\n372\t          \"95% CI\",\n373\t          \"Interpretation\"\n374\t        ],\n375\t        \"rows\": [\n376\t          [\n377\t            \"Sample baseline perplexity (340M h0)\",\n378\t            0.48,\n379\t            \"[0.39, 0.56]\",\n380\t            \"Harder samples rebound more\"\n381\t          ],\n382\t          [\n383\t            \"Sample baseline perplexity (1.3B h0)\",\n384\t            0.22,\n385\t            \"[0.12, 0.32]\",\n386\t            \"Effect present but weaker at scale\"\n387\t          ],\n388\t          [\n389\t            \"Perplexity ratio (340M/1.3B)\",\n390\t            0.31,\n391\t            \"[0.20, 0.41]\",\n392\t            \"Confounded — captures both scale and training data effects\"\n393\t          ]\n394\t        ]\n395\t      }\n396\t    ],\n397\t    \"figures\": [],\n398\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-007 的 median 结果为 Claim 2 提供了 \\\"比 aggregate 更深但不完美\\\" 的证据——恰好符合 EMNLP Findings 的期望水平。rebound-hardest-samples overlap (62%) 是一个 informative finding， 给出了直觉上合理的 capacity saturation 解释。但 training token confound 无法 fully disentangle 是一个 honest limitation。论文措辞建议：\\\"Scale is a necessary condition for complete convergence, likely through increased capacity to jointly optimize recurrence and attention; however, the co-varying training data volume (20B vs 100B tokens) prevents definitive attribution to parameter count alone.\\\" 这种 careful framing 对 EMNLP 审稿人来说是可接受的。\\n\\n\\nmedian 档预测 rebound 被 \\\"部分解释\\\"。340M 在高 attention ratio 处的 rebound (std 回升) 与 最困难样本高度重叠 (62%)：这些样本需要模型同时执行 retrieval 和 integration，当 attention layers 占据了过多容量 (8/12 layers) 时，340M 的有限参数无法同时维持 recurrence quality 和 attention quality， 产生 capacity saturation。1.3B 有足够参数避免这个瓶颈。 但 training tokens 的 5x 差异 (20B vs 100B) 是无法完全 disentangle 的 confound： 更多的训练数据可能让 1.3B 学到了更好的 attention-recurrence 协调模式，而不仅仅是 scale 带来的 capacity 优势。相关性分析 (r=0.31) 表明两种因素都在起作用但无法分离。 论文必须在 Claim 2 中增加 explicit limitation paragraph 说明这个 confound。\\n\"\n399\t  },\n400\t  {\n401\t    \"name\": \"Statistical robustness framework\",\n402\t    \"description\": \"对核心 convergence metrics 实施 bootstrap CI, Bonferroni/FDR 多重比较校正,  GDN-excluded sensitivity analysis, 以及 effect size (Cohen's d / η²) 报告。\\n\",\n403\t    \"results\": {\n404\t      \"lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_mean_pct\": 77,\n405\t      \"lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci95\": [\n406\t        68,\n407\t        84\n408\t      ],\n409\t      \"lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci95_lower\": 0.68,\n410\t      \"lambada_std_reduction_gdn_excluded_pct\": 38,\n411\t      \"lambada_std_reduction_gdn_excluded_ci95\": [\n412\t        22,\n413\t        53\n414\t      ],\n415\t      \"lambada_std_reduction_gdn_excluded_ci95_lower\": 0.22,\n416\t      \"gdn_excluded_pairwise_convergence_direction\": \"holds (RetNet-HGRN2 std decreases with attention)\",\n417\t      \"gdn_excluded_convergence_p\": 0.042,\n418\t      \"gdn_excluded_convergence_rho\": -0.9,\n419\t      \"bonferroni_lambada_p_adjusted\": 0.048,\n420\t      \"bonferroni_n_significant_after_correction\": 1,\n421\t      \"fdr_n_significant_after_correction\": 1,\n422\t      \"cohens_d_lambada_h0_vs_h24\": 1.82,\n423\t      \"cohens_d_arc_easy_h0_vs_h24\": 0.45,\n424\t      \"eta_squared_attention_ratio_on_std\": 0.71,\n425\t      \"all_core_claims_survive_gdn_excluded\": true,\n426\t      \"effect_sizes_shrink_gdn_excluded\": true,\n427\t      \"effect_size_shrink_factor\": \"~50% reduction in std reduction metric\"\n428\t    },\n429\t    \"tables\": [\n430\t      {\n431\t        \"title\": \"Table: Bootstrap confidence intervals for convergence metrics\",\n432\t        \"columns\": [\n433\t          \"Metric\",\n434\t          \"Point Estimate\",\n435\t          \"Bootstrap 95% CI\",\n436\t          \"GDN-Excluded Estimate\",\n437\t          \"GDN-Excluded 95% CI\"\n438\t        ],\n439\t        \"rows\": [\n440\t          [\n441\t            \"LAMBADA std reduction %\",\n442\t            \"79%\",\n443\t            \"[68%, 84%]\",\n444\t            \"38%\",\n445\t            \"[22%, 53%]\"\n446\t          ],\n447\t          [\n448\t            \"LAMBADA convergence ρ\",\n449\t            -1.0,\n450\t            \"[-1.0, -0.90]\",\n451\t            -0.9,\n452\t            \"[-1.0, -0.60]\"\n453\t          ],\n454\t          [\n455\t            \"ARC-E std reduction %\",\n456\t            \"38%\",\n457\t            \"[15%, 55%]\",\n458\t            \"25%\",\n459\t            \"[5%, 44%]\"\n460\t          ],\n461\t          [\n462\t            \"Cross-benchmark dose-response ρ\",\n463\t            -0.66,\n464\t            \"[-0.89, -0.31]\",\n465\t            -0.55,\n466\t            \"[-0.88, -0.10]\"\n467\t          ]\n468\t        ],\n469\t        \"notes\": \"Bootstrap: 10,000 resamples. GDN-excluded: n=2 architectures (RetNet, HGRN2) with 5 attention ratios each.\"\n470\t      },\n471\t      {\n472\t        \"title\": \"Table: Multiple comparison correction\",\n473\t        \"columns\": [\n474\t          \"Benchmark\",\n475\t          \"Raw p\",\n476\t          \"Bonferroni p (×6)\",\n477\t          \"FDR q\",\n478\t          \"Significant after correction?\"\n479\t        ],\n480\t        \"rows\": [\n481\t          [\n482\t            \"LAMBADA\",\n483\t            0.008,\n484\t            0.048,\n485\t            0.048,\n486\t            \"Yes (borderline)\"\n487\t          ],\n488\t          [\n489\t            \"ARC-Easy\",\n490\t            0.117,\n491\t            0.702,\n492\t            0.351,\n493\t            \"No\"\n494\t          ],\n495\t          [\n496\t            \"MMLU\",\n497\t            0.117,\n498\t            0.702,\n499\t            0.351,\n500\t            \"No\"\n501\t          ],\n502\t          [\n503\t            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n504\t            0.624,\n505\t            1.0,\n506\t            0.749,\n507\t            \"No\"\n508\t          ],\n509\t          [\n510\t            \"WinoGrande\",\n511\t            0.608,\n512\t            1.0,\n513\t            0.749,\n514\t            \"No\"\n515\t          ],\n516\t          [\n517\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n518\t            0.742,\n519\t            1.0,\n520\t            0.742,\n521\t            \"No\"\n522\t          ]\n523\t        ]\n524\t      },\n525\t      {\n526\t        \"title\": \"Table: Effect sizes\",\n527\t        \"columns\": [\n528\t          \"Comparison\",\n529\t          \"Cohen's d\",\n530\t          \"η²\",\n531\t          \"Interpretation\"\n532\t        ],\n533\t        \"rows\": [\n534\t          [\n535\t            \"LAMBADA cross-arch std: h0 vs h24-1\",\n536\t            1.82,\n537\t            \"—\",\n538\t            \"Large\"\n539\t          ],\n540\t          [\n541\t            \"LAMBADA attention ratio → std (ANOVA)\",\n542\t            \"—\",\n543\t            0.71,\n544\t            \"Large\"\n545\t          ],\n546\t          [\n547\t            \"ARC-E cross-arch std: h0 vs h24-1\",\n548\t            0.45,\n549\t            \"—\",\n550\t            \"Small-Medium\"\n551\t          ],\n552\t          [\n553\t            \"HellaSwag cross-arch std: h0 vs h24-1\",\n554\t            0.08,\n555\t            \"—\",\n556\t            \"Negligible\"\n557\t          ]\n558\t        ]\n559\t      }\n560\t    ],\n561\t    \"figures\": [],\n562\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-008 是 median 档论文的 statistical backbone。核心 message：effect 是 real 且 large on LAMBADA， 但 scope is narrow (only LAMBADA survives correction)，且 robustness to GDN exclusion shows effect sizes shrink substantially (38% vs 79%)。 审稿人会 appreciate 这种 self-critical rigor。GDN-excluded CI lower bound = 22% 意味着即使在 most conservative scenario 下仍有 meaningful convergence，但不是 \\\"dramatic\\\"。 关键写作策略：把 Bonferroni-significant-only-LAMBADA 框架为 \\\"our conservative test confirms the retrieval-gated nature of the effect\\\" 而非 \\\"we failed to find significance elsewhere\\\"。 Effect size table 对 Meta-analysis 友好，审稿人 D 会满意。\\n\\n\\nmedian 档的关键约束是 GDN-excluded 后 effect size 大幅缩水但 directionally survive。 原因：GDN 是三个架构中 convergence 效应最强的（从 aggregate 角度，GDN 在高 attention ratio 时 与其他两个最接近），移除它后跨架构 variance 的基线本身就变小（RetNet 和 HGRN2 的 h0 性能差异 比 GDN 参与时小），导致 std reduction 百分比从 79% 降至 38%。Bootstrap CI 变宽是因为 n=2 architectures 的 pairwise comparison 本质上自由度极低。 但 directional survival 是可信的：RetNet-HGRN2 pair 在 LAMBADA 上确实随 attention 增加而收敛 (ρ=-0.90, p=0.042)，只是 magnitude 更小。 Bonferroni 校正后只有 LAMBADA 存活 (0.008×6=0.048)，这在 median 档下是 expected—— 不改变 \\\"LAMBADA-anchored\\\" 的叙事，反而为 honest scope 提供了 formal justification。 Cohen's d=1.82 (LAMBADA h0 vs h24) 表明 effect size 本身是 large 的；问题不在 \\\"是否存在\\\" 而在 \\\"范围多广\\\"。\\n\"\n563\t  },\n564\t  {\n565\t    \"name\": \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\",\n566\t    \"description\": \"对 LAMBADA，将 aggregate convergence curve 与 per-example divergence metrics  (Jaccard, net effect asymmetry) 作为 attention ratio 的函数并列绘制， 展示 convergence 和 divergence 共同演化——attention 越多，aggregate 越收敛但 per-example 越分化。\\n\",\n567\t    \"results\": {\n568\t      \"convergence_divergence_correlation_rho\": -0.85,\n569\t      \"convergence_divergence_correlation_p\": 0.033,\n570\t      \"convergence_metric\": \"cross-arch std of LAMBADA accuracy\",\n571\t      \"divergence_metric\": \"mean pairwise Jaccard of helped sets (lower = more divergent)\",\n572\t      \"co_evolution_pattern\": \"as attention ratio increases 0→24, cross-arch std decreases monotonically while mean Jaccard also decreases (more architecture-specific effects)\",\n573\t      \"jaccard_at_h0\": 0.15,\n574\t      \"jaccard_at_h3\": 0.1,\n575\t      \"jaccard_at_h6\": 0.08,\n576\t      \"jaccard_at_h12\": 0.07,\n577\t      \"jaccard_at_h24\": 0.06,\n578\t      \"std_at_h0\": 0.024,\n579\t      \"std_at_h3\": 0.015,\n580\t      \"std_at_h6\": 0.01,\n581\t      \"std_at_h12\": 0.007,\n582\t      \"std_at_h24\": 0.005,\n583\t      \"net_effect_asymmetry_gdn_trend\": \"increasingly negative (more hurt) with attention\",\n584\t      \"net_effect_asymmetry_hgrn2_trend\": \"increasingly positive (more helped) with attention\",\n585\t      \"net_effect_asymmetry_retnet_trend\": \"slightly negative, relatively stable\",\n586\t      \"paradox_strength_at_max_attention\": \"strongest — maximum aggregate convergence coexists with minimum per-example overlap\"\n587\t    },\n588\t    \"tables\": [\n589\t      {\n590\t        \"title\": \"Table: Convergence-divergence co-evolution across attention ratios (LAMBADA, 1.3B)\",\n591\t        \"columns\": [\n592\t          \"Attention Ratio\",\n593\t          \"Cross-Arch Std\",\n594\t          \"Mean Pairwise Jaccard (Helped)\",\n595\t          \"GDN Net Effect\",\n596\t          \"HGRN2 Net Effect\",\n597\t          \"RetNet Net Effect\"\n598\t        ],\n599\t        \"rows\": [\n600\t          [\n601\t            \"h0 (0/12)\",\n602\t            0.024,\n603\t            0.15,\n604\t            0,\n605\t            0,\n606\t            0\n607\t          ],\n608\t          [\n609\t            \"h3-1 (3/12)\",\n610\t            0.015,\n611\t            0.1,\n612\t            -52,\n613\t            48,\n614\t            -18\n615\t          ],\n616\t          [\n617\t            \"h6-1 (6/12)\",\n618\t            0.01,\n619\t            0.08,\n620\t            -98,\n621\t            105,\n622\t            -35\n623\t          ],\n624\t          [\n625\t            \"h12-1 (12/12)\",\n626\t            0.007,\n627\t            0.07,\n628\t            -130,\n629\t            138,\n630\t            -52\n631\t          ],\n632\t          [\n633\t            \"h24-1 (24/24)\",\n634\t            0.005,\n635\t            0.06,\n636\t            -153,\n637\t            153,\n638\t            -69\n639\t          ]\n640\t        ],\n641\t        \"notes\": \"Net Effect = helped_count - hurt_count on LAMBADA. h0 has no attention, so net effects are 0 (baseline). Jaccard at h0 reflects residual overlap from different random initializations.\"\n642\t      }\n643\t    ],\n644\t    \"figures\": [],\n645\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-010 产出论文最重要的 figure——dual-axis convergence-divergence plot。ρ=-0.85 (p=0.033)  是 median 档论文中最 \\\"clean\\\" 的统计结果之一（仅次于 LAMBADA 的 ρ=-1.0），因为它在单个 benchmark  内利用了 attention ratio 的 5 个梯度点，避免了跨 benchmark dose-response 的 low-n 问题。 这个 figure 同时服务于 Claim 1 (aggregate convergence) 和 Claim 3 (per-example divergence)， 是连接两个 claims 的 bridge evidence。 论文结构建议：在 Results 中先展示 aggregate convergence (Claim 1)，再展示 per-example divergence  (Claim 3)，最后用 exp-010 figure 作为 \\\"synthesis\\\" 展示两者的 co-evolution—— 这就是 \\\"equalizer paradox\\\" 的完整呈现。\\n\\nconvergence-divergence co-evolution 是 equalizer paradox 的核心可视化。在 median 档下， 相关性 ρ=-0.85 (p=0.033) 是显著的——这是 n=5 attention ratios 的 rank correlation， 比跨 benchmark 的 dose-response 有更好的 power（因为这里 both metrics 在同一 benchmark 内变化）。 机制直觉：attention 层越多，每个架构能 \\\"选择性优化\\\" 的样本子集越大，但这些子集由架构内部结构 决定因此互不重叠。GDN 的 delta rule 在高 attention 下更多地 \\\"依赖\\\" attention 来处理精确 retrieval， 但这牺牲了 delta rule 对某些样本的原生优势（hurt 增加）；HGRN2 的 hierarchical gating 与 attention 更互补，所以随 attention 增加变得 increasingly helped。最终 aggregate 收敛是因为三个架构 通过不同路径到达了相似的 accuracy level——但路径本身越来越不同。 Jaccard 从 0.15 (h0) 降至 0.06 (h24) 表明 h0 时 helped/hurt sets 本身就有低重叠 （这可能部分反映 baseline noise），attention 增加后进一步分化。\\n\"\n646\t  }\n647\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7ff5ff9-a534-4909-96dd-e2798498e0e9","uuid":"bbea52f0-9718-4df5-a186-c87d540c3706","timestamp":"2026-05-19T14:08:08.302Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T135121/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis (task-specificity validation)\",\n    \"description\": \"Re-run lm-eval with --log_samples on 1.3B models (GDN, RetNet, HGRN2 at h0/h3-1/h6-1/h12-1/h24-1) for HellaSwag, ARC-Easy, ARC-Challenge. Also collect 340M RetNet+HGRN2 (10 models) and 1.3B GDN h3-1/h6-1/h24-1 missing configs. Compute per-example helped/hurt sets, pairwise Jaccard, and per-example convergence metrics analogous to LAMBADA analysis.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"hellaswag_per_example_convergence\": false,\n      \"hellaswag_jaccard_cross_arch_mean\": 0.18,\n      \"hellaswag_jaccard_interpretation\": \"near-random overlap, no systematic pattern\",\n      \"hellaswag_helped_hurt_net_direction\": \"inconsistent across architectures and attention ratios\",\n      \"arc_easy_per_example_convergence\": \"noisy/suggestive\",\n      \"arc_easy_jaccard_cross_arch_mean\": 0.12,\n      \"arc_easy_std_reduction_pct\": 38,\n      \"arc_easy_std_reduction_p\": 0.14,\n      \"arc_easy_helped_hurt_asymmetry\": \"present but unstable across attention ratios\",\n      \"arc_challenge_per_example_convergence\": false,\n      \"arc_challenge_jaccard_cross_arch_mean\": 0.15,\n      \"arc_challenge_std_reduction_pct\": 12,\n      \"dose_response_rho_6benchmarks\": -0.66,\n      \"dose_response_rho_p\": 0.16,\n      \"n_benchmarks_per_example_confirmed_converging\": 1,\n      \"n_benchmarks_suggestive\": 1,\n      \"n_benchmarks_confirmed_non_converging\": 4,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Per-example convergence metrics across benchmarks (1.3B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Retrieval Demand\",\n          \"Aggregate ρ (std vs attn)\",\n          \"Aggregate p\",\n          \"Per-example Jaccard (mean pairwise)\",\n          \"Std Reduction %\",\n          \"Per-example Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA\",\n            \"High\",\n            -1.0,\n            0.008,\n            0.08,\n            \"79%\",\n            \"Converging (architecture-specific mechanism)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Easy\",\n            \"Medium\",\n            -0.7,\n            0.117,\n            0.12,\n            \"38%\",\n            \"Noisy/suggestive\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            \"Low-Medium\",\n            -0.3,\n            0.624,\n            0.15,\n            \"12%\",\n            \"Non-converging\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            \"Low\",\n            0.3,\n            0.742,\n            0.18,\n            \"-5%\",\n            \"Non-converging (confirmed per-example)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"WinoGrande\",\n            \"Low*\",\n            0.1,\n            0.608,\n            \"N/A†\",\n            \"3%\",\n            \"Non-converging\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"Mixed\",\n            -0.7,\n            0.117,\n            \"N/A†\",\n            \"22%\",\n            \"Unclear (aggregate suggestive, no per-example data)\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"†Per-example data not collected for WinoGrande/MMLU in this experiment. *WinoGrande has coreference retrieval component; acknowledged in text.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-002 的 median 结果确认 task-specificity 是真实的，但把 \\\"dose-response\\\" 的统计力量限制在了 descriptive level。论文的关键修辞策略：不要声称 dose-response 是 \\\"established\\\"，而是用 \\\"consistent with a retrieval-demand gradient\\\" + \\\"preliminary due to limited benchmark-level n\\\" 的措辞。 HellaSwag per-example 确认非收敛这一点很有价值——把 aggregate p=0.742 升级为 \\\"per-example confirmed non-converging\\\"，排除了 \\\"aggregate 不显著只是因为 power 不够\\\" 的可能性。 ARC-E 的 noisy 结果实际上对叙事有利：它不是 retrieval 纯任务，所以 partial/noisy convergence 正好符合 \\\"retrieval demand 越高收敛越强\\\" 的 gradient story。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档下，equalizer effect 本质上是 retrieval-gated 的。LAMBADA 是纯粹的 last-word retrieval 任务， attention 机制对此类任务有直接的结构性优势（回看上下文定位 target word），因此 per-example 收敛清晰。 ARC-Easy 包含部分 retrieval 成分（从选项中匹配已知事实），但混合了推理成分，导致 per-example 层面噪声大—— Jaccard 结构模糊，helped/hurt 集合随 attention ratio 变化不稳定，aggregate std 降低存在但不显著。 HellaSwag 和 ARC-Challenge 主要依赖 commonsense reasoning 和 multi-step inference，attention 的贡献 分散在多种推理路径上而非集中在 retrieval 上，因此 per-example 分析确认了 aggregate 层面的非收敛： 不同架构被 attention 帮助/伤害的样本几乎是随机的，无系统性结构。 这使 dose-response 本质上变成了 2-point gradient：LAMBADA 强，ARC-E suggestive，其余 flat。 6 个 benchmark 的 Spearman ρ≈-0.66（在 [-0.75, -0.55] 范围内）但因 n=6 且非线性分布，p≈0.16 不显著—— 这足以支持 \\\"retrieval demand 调节收敛强度\\\" 的叙事，但必须承认是 preliminary observation 而非 established relationship。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Helped/hurt sample characterization Phase 2 (perplexity + topic/domain)\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Phase 1 surface features 全部 non-significant 的基础上，Phase 2 测试更深层特征： (a) 各架构 pure recurrent baseline (h0) 下每个 LAMBADA 样本的 perplexity， (b) 基于 LAMBADA 文本内容的 topic/domain 分布 (LDA 或预训练 topic model)。 检验 helped/hurt 样本是否在这些特征上可区分。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"perplexity_gdn_helped_vs_hurt_p\": 0.031,\n      \"perplexity_gdn_helped_vs_hurt_cohens_d\": 0.19,\n      \"perplexity_gdn_direction\": \"hurt samples have higher baseline perplexity (harder under pure recurrence)\",\n      \"perplexity_hgrn2_helped_vs_hurt_p\": 0.22,\n      \"perplexity_hgrn2_helped_vs_hurt_cohens_d\": 0.08,\n      \"perplexity_retnet_helped_vs_hurt_p\": 0.09,\n      \"perplexity_retnet_helped_vs_hurt_cohens_d\": 0.13,\n      \"topic_gdn_chi2_p\": 0.34,\n      \"topic_hgrn2_chi2_p\": 0.51,\n      \"topic_retnet_chi2_p\": 0.28,\n      \"cross_arch_perplexity_interaction_p\": 0.07,\n      \"n_features_significant_any_arch\": 1,\n      \"n_features_significant_cross_arch\": 0,\n      \"overall_mechanism_status\": \"opaque to tested features; perplexity suggestive for GDN only\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Phase 2 feature analysis — helped vs hurt sample characterization\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Feature\",\n          \"Architecture\",\n          \"Test\",\n          \"p-value\",\n          \"Effect Size (d/V)\",\n          \"Direction\",\n          \"Significant?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Baseline perplexity (h0)\",\n            \"GDN\",\n            \"Mann-Whitney U\",\n            0.031,\n            \"d=0.19\",\n            \"Hurt > Helped\",\n            \"Marginal*\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Baseline perplexity (h0)\",\n            \"HGRN2\",\n            \"Mann-Whitney U\",\n            0.22,\n            \"d=0.08\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Baseline perplexity (h0)\",\n            \"RetNet\",\n            \"Mann-Whitney U\",\n            0.09,\n            \"d=0.13\",\n            \"Hurt > Helped (trend)\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Topic distribution\",\n            \"GDN\",\n            \"Chi-squared\",\n            0.34,\n            \"V=0.06\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Topic distribution\",\n            \"HGRN2\",\n            \"Chi-squared\",\n            0.51,\n            \"V=0.04\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Topic distribution\",\n            \"RetNet\",\n            \"Chi-squared\",\n            0.28,\n            \"V=0.07\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Perplexity × Arch interaction\",\n            \"All\",\n            \"Two-way ANOVA\",\n            0.07,\n            \"η²=0.003\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"No (trend)\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"*Marginal: 0.01 < p < 0.05, below preregistered p<0.01 threshold for individual tests. After Bonferroni correction (6 tests), adjusted p=0.186.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Phase 2 的 GDN perplexity signal (p=0.031) 在论文中的定位需要谨慎：它通过了 nominal 0.05 但 未通过 preregistered 0.01，且 Bonferroni 校正后不显著。论文应报告为 \\\"suggestive lead for future work\\\"， 不作为 claimed finding。关键叙事价值在负面结果的累积：surface features (Phase 1) + perplexity + topic 全部失败或 marginal，系统性地排除了从简单到中等复杂度的解释，让 \\\"mechanism is opaque\\\" 不是一句空话 而是有实证支撑的 negative characterization。这对 EMNLP Findings 审稿人来说是可接受的—— 他们会 appreciate careful negative results over overclaimed positive ones。\\n\\n\\nmedian 档的核心假设是 mechanism 保持 opaque。Phase 2 的 perplexity 特征比 surface features 更有信息量， 因为它直接衡量 \\\"pure recurrence 下的困难度\\\"——直觉上，attention 最可能帮助那些 recurrence 本身处理不好的样本。 但这个直觉只在一个架构 (GDN) 上得到 marginal 验证 (p=0.031, d=0.19)：GDN 的 gated delta rule 机制 在高 perplexity 样本上可能有特定的弱点（例如需要精确的长距离 copy 但 delta rule 的 memory update 不够精确），attention 填补了这个缺口。HGRN2 和 RetNet 的 hierarchical/exponential decay 机制 处理困难样本的方式不同，perplexity 不是它们的瓶颈维度，所以信号消失。 Topic/domain 特征完全 non-significant：attention 的效果不是 \\\"对某些 domain 更有用\\\"， 而是在每个 domain 内部都有 architecture-specific 的帮助/伤害模式。 这实际上强化了 \\\"opaque mechanism\\\" 的叙事——连中间层特征 (perplexity) 也只给出了微弱线索， 说明 equalizer effect 的机制深嵌在 recurrence-attention 交互的计算层面。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\",\n    \"description\": \"提取 3 个架构 h3-1 配置的 attention weight patterns (1.3B)。 在 LAMBADA 样本上计算：(a) attention 聚焦位置分布，(b) attention pattern 与 helped/hurt 身份的相关性， (c) 跨架构 attention pattern 相似度。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gdn_attention_entropy_mean\": 3.2,\n      \"hgrn2_attention_entropy_mean\": 2.8,\n      \"retnet_attention_entropy_mean\": 3.0,\n      \"attention_focus_on_target_context_pct_gdn\": 0.42,\n      \"attention_focus_on_target_context_pct_hgrn2\": 0.58,\n      \"attention_focus_on_target_context_pct_retnet\": 0.47,\n      \"cross_arch_attention_cosine_similarity_mean\": 0.35,\n      \"attention_pattern_correlation_with_helped_gdn\": 0.18,\n      \"attention_pattern_correlation_with_helped_hgrn2\": 0.27,\n      \"attention_pattern_correlation_with_helped_retnet\": 0.22,\n      \"attention_pattern_correlation_mean\": 0.22,\n      \"passes_preregistered_threshold\": false,\n      \"qualitative_patterns_visible\": true,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 3.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Attention pattern analysis summary (h3-1 config, 1.3B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Architecture\",\n          \"Attn Entropy (mean)\",\n          \"Target Context Focus %\",\n          \"Corr with Helped/Hurt (r)\",\n          \"Corr p-value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GDN\",\n            3.2,\n            \"42%\",\n            0.18,\n            0.002\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HGRN2\",\n            2.8,\n            \"58%\",\n            0.27,\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RetNet\",\n            3.0,\n            \"47%\",\n            0.22,\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"All correlations significant due to large n (>900 samples) but effect sizes below preregistered r>0.3 threshold. Target Context Focus = fraction of attention weight on tokens within 10-token window preceding target word.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Cross-architecture attention pattern similarity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Architecture Pair\",\n          \"Cosine Similarity (mean)\",\n          \"Similarity on Helped Samples\",\n          \"Similarity on Hurt Samples\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GDN–HGRN2\",\n            0.31,\n            0.28,\n            0.33\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GDN–RetNet\",\n            0.38,\n            0.35,\n            0.4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HGRN2–RetNet\",\n            0.36,\n            0.32,\n            0.39\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"Similarity computed on attention weight vectors averaged over heads and layers. Low similarity consistent with architecture-specific attention usage.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-004 的 median 结果产出两类价值：(1) 定性 illustration 素材（attention heatmap triptych 将成为论文最直观的 figure，直接展示 \\\"same input, different attention patterns\\\" 的 paradox）， (2) 进一步的 negative quantitative evidence 强化 \\\"opaque mechanism\\\" 叙事。 关键措辞：attention pattern 与 helped/hurt 有 \\\"detectable but weak association\\\" (r≈0.22)， 说明 attention 的作用不完全随机，但远不足以 predict 或 explain 哪些样本被帮助/伤害。 这与 Phase 2 perplexity 的 marginal signal 形成呼应——mechanism 有线索但不可解。 审稿人 Concern C (\\\"No causal mechanism\\\") 的回应变为：\\\"We provide three levels of mechanistic evidence — all suggestive, none conclusive — establishing the phenomenon's depth.\\\"\\n\\n\\nmedian 档预测 attention correlation r=0.15–0.30，低于 preregistered r>0.3 threshold。 原因在于 attention 的作用路径是间接的：attention layer 不仅直接影响输出 logits， 还通过修改 hidden state 影响后续 recurrent layers 的计算。因此 attention weight pattern 本身只捕获了 \\\"attention 在看什么\\\" 而非 \\\"attention 如何改变了下游计算\\\"。 具体来说：HGRN2 的 hierarchical gating 与 attention 有最强的协同 (r=0.27)，因为 HGRN2 的层级结构天然需要不同粒度的信息，attention 提供的全局视野与其互补性最强；GDN 的 delta rule 更新机制与 attention 的交互更复杂 (r=0.18)，因为 delta rule 的精确 memory 操作可能 在某些层 override attention 的影响。 定性上，attention heatmap 会显示有趣的模式：例如 HGRN2 的 attention 更集中在 sentence boundaries 和 target-word context windows，而 GDN 的 attention 更分散——但这些差异在统计检验中被 样本间噪声淹没。论文中作为 qualitative illustration 展示，配合 \\\"future work: causal intervention on attention weights\\\" 的讨论。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Architecture expansion check\",\n    \"description\": \"搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 及公开 repos (HuggingFace, GitHub) 寻找额外的 hybrid 架构 (Mamba/Mamba2 hybrid, RWKV hybrid, Griffin, etc.)。如果找到，在 LAMBADA 上评估收敛模式。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"additional_architectures_found\": 0,\n      \"mamba_hybrid_status\": \"no Wang et al. equivalent; community checkpoints exist but different training setup (not comparable)\",\n      \"rwkv_hybrid_status\": \"RWKV-6 hybrid mentioned in literature but no public 1.3B checkpoint with matched attention ratios\",\n      \"griffin_status\": \"Google proprietary, no public weights\",\n      \"search_exhaustive\": true,\n      \"n_architectures_final\": 3,\n      \"mitigation_framing\": \"3 architectures represent 3 distinct recurrence mechanisms (gated delta rule, linear attention + exp decay, hierarchical gated recurrence); acknowledged as limitation\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-005 的 null result 对论文的影响是 Limitations 段必须明确写 \\\"n=3 architectures\\\" 并 呼吁社区建立更大的 standardized hybrid model zoo。这是审稿人 Concern D 的直接回应。 在 median 档下，审稿人可能把这作为 \\\"not Main, push to Findings\\\" 的理由之一， 但不太可能因此 reject——因为 per-example analysis 的 novelty 不依赖架构数量。\\n\\n\\nmedian 档假设找不到额外可比架构。Wang et al. 的 model zoo 是目前最全面的 hybrid 架构实验—— 他们选择 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 正是因为这三个有公开实现且代表了三大类 recurrence 机制。 Mamba hybrid (Jamba) 由 AI21 发布但训练 setup 完全不同（不同数据、不同 tokenizer、不同规模点）， 不能直接加入 controlled comparison。RWKV hybrid 讨论较多但标准化的 attention ratio sweep checkpoint 不存在。Griffin 是 Google 的 proprietary architecture。 n=3 在 median 档下必须诚实承认为 limitation，但论文可以辩护：per-example analysis 提供了 上千个 data points，三个架构覆盖了三种根本不同的 recurrence 机制，且 convergence 效应在 所有三个上都观测到——这不是 \\\"cherry-picked 一个能 work 的架构\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"深入分析 340M 在 attn=8 处的非单调 rebound。与 1.3B 同 attention ratio 进行 per-example 比较， 识别 diverging samples。分析 training token count (20B vs 100B) 作为 confound。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rebound_samples_overlap_with_hardest_pct\": 62,\n      \"rebound_samples_overlap_with_hardest_ci95\": [\n        48,\n        74\n      ],\n      \"hardest_definition\": \"bottom 20% accuracy under 340M h0 baseline\",\n      \"rebound_at_1_3b_same_ratio\": \"no rebound (monotonic convergence continues)\",\n      \"scale_delta_explanation_pct\": 45,\n      \"scale_delta_explanation\": \"340M rebound partially explained by capacity saturation on hard samples\",\n      \"training_token_confound_disentangled\": false,\n      \"training_token_analysis\": \"340M trained on 20B tokens, 1.3B on 100B tokens; rebound samples have higher perplexity under both scales but magnitude differs; cannot separate scale vs data effects\",\n      \"confound_correlation_with_rebound\": 0.31,\n      \"mechanism_confidence\": \"partial — capacity explanation plausible but token confound unresolved\",\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 1.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: 340M rebound analysis — sample characterization\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Sample Group\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"340M h0 Acc\",\n          \"340M h8 Acc\",\n          \"1.3B h0 Acc\",\n          \"1.3B h8 Acc\",\n          \"Rebound?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Rebound samples (340M)\",\n            187,\n            \"31%\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"52%\",\n            \"61%\",\n            \"Yes at 340M, No at 1.3B\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Non-rebound samples (340M)\",\n            4926,\n            \"78%\",\n            \"82%\",\n            \"85%\",\n            \"89%\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Overlap with hardest 20%\",\n            \"116/187 (62%)\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"Rebound samples defined as those with accuracy drop from h6 to h8 at 340M. Hardest 20% = bottom quintile of h0 accuracy.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Training token confound assessment\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Factor\",\n          \"Correlation with Rebound Magnitude\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Sample baseline perplexity (340M h0)\",\n            0.48,\n            \"[0.39, 0.56]\",\n            \"Harder samples rebound more\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Sample baseline perplexity (1.3B h0)\",\n            0.22,\n            \"[0.12, 0.32]\",\n            \"Effect present but weaker at scale\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Perplexity ratio (340M/1.3B)\",\n            0.31,\n            \"[0.20, 0.41]\",\n            \"Confounded — captures both scale and training data effects\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-007 的 median 结果为 Claim 2 提供了 \\\"比 aggregate 更深但不完美\\\" 的证据——恰好符合 EMNLP Findings 的期望水平。rebound-hardest-samples overlap (62%) 是一个 informative finding， 给出了直觉上合理的 capacity saturation 解释。但 training token confound 无法 fully disentangle 是一个 honest limitation。论文措辞建议：\\\"Scale is a necessary condition for complete convergence, likely through increased capacity to jointly optimize recurrence and attention; however, the co-varying training data volume (20B vs 100B tokens) prevents definitive attribution to parameter count alone.\\\" 这种 careful framing 对 EMNLP 审稿人来说是可接受的。\\n\\n\\nmedian 档预测 rebound 被 \\\"部分解释\\\"。340M 在高 attention ratio 处的 rebound (std 回升) 与 最困难样本高度重叠 (62%)：这些样本需要模型同时执行 retrieval 和 integration，当 attention layers 占据了过多容量 (8/12 layers) 时，340M 的有限参数无法同时维持 recurrence quality 和 attention quality， 产生 capacity saturation。1.3B 有足够参数避免这个瓶颈。 但 training tokens 的 5x 差异 (20B vs 100B) 是无法完全 disentangle 的 confound： 更多的训练数据可能让 1.3B 学到了更好的 attention-recurrence 协调模式，而不仅仅是 scale 带来的 capacity 优势。相关性分析 (r=0.31) 表明两种因素都在起作用但无法分离。 论文必须在 Claim 2 中增加 explicit limitation paragraph 说明这个 confound。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Statistical robustness framework\",\n    \"description\": \"对核心 convergence metrics 实施 bootstrap CI, Bonferroni/FDR 多重比较校正,  GDN-excluded sensitivity analysis, 以及 effect size (Cohen's d / η²) 报告。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_mean_pct\": 77,\n      \"lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci95\": [\n        68,\n        84\n      ],\n      \"lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci95_lower\": 0.68,\n      \"lambada_std_reduction_gdn_excluded_pct\": 38,\n      \"lambada_std_reduction_gdn_excluded_ci95\": [\n        22,\n        53\n      ],\n      \"lambada_std_reduction_gdn_excluded_ci95_lower\": 0.22,\n      \"gdn_excluded_pairwise_convergence_direction\": \"holds (RetNet-HGRN2 std decreases with attention)\",\n      \"gdn_excluded_convergence_p\": 0.042,\n      \"gdn_excluded_convergence_rho\": -0.9,\n      \"bonferroni_lambada_p_adjusted\": 0.048,\n      \"bonferroni_n_significant_after_correction\": 1,\n      \"fdr_n_significant_after_correction\": 1,\n      \"cohens_d_lambada_h0_vs_h24\": 1.82,\n      \"cohens_d_arc_easy_h0_vs_h24\": 0.45,\n      \"eta_squared_attention_ratio_on_std\": 0.71,\n      \"all_core_claims_survive_gdn_excluded\": true,\n      \"effect_sizes_shrink_gdn_excluded\": true,\n      \"effect_size_shrink_factor\": \"~50% reduction in std reduction metric\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Bootstrap confidence intervals for convergence metrics\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Point Estimate\",\n          \"Bootstrap 95% CI\",\n          \"GDN-Excluded Estimate\",\n          \"GDN-Excluded 95% CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA std reduction %\",\n            \"79%\",\n            \"[68%, 84%]\",\n            \"38%\",\n            \"[22%, 53%]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA convergence ρ\",\n            -1.0,\n            \"[-1.0, -0.90]\",\n            -0.9,\n            \"[-1.0, -0.60]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-E std reduction %\",\n            \"38%\",\n            \"[15%, 55%]\",\n            \"25%\",\n            \"[5%, 44%]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cross-benchmark dose-response ρ\",\n            -0.66,\n            \"[-0.89, -0.31]\",\n            -0.55,\n            \"[-0.88, -0.10]\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"Bootstrap: 10,000 resamples. GDN-excluded: n=2 architectures (RetNet, HGRN2) with 5 attention ratios each.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Multiple comparison correction\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Raw p\",\n          \"Bonferroni p (×6)\",\n          \"FDR q\",\n          \"Significant after correction?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA\",\n            0.008,\n            0.048,\n            0.048,\n            \"Yes (borderline)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Easy\",\n            0.117,\n            0.702,\n            0.351,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.117,\n            0.702,\n            0.351,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            0.624,\n            1.0,\n            0.749,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"WinoGrande\",\n            0.608,\n            1.0,\n            0.749,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            0.742,\n            1.0,\n            0.742,\n            \"No\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Effect sizes\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Comparison\",\n          \"Cohen's d\",\n          \"η²\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA cross-arch std: h0 vs h24-1\",\n            1.82,\n            \"—\",\n            \"Large\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA attention ratio → std (ANOVA)\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.71,\n            \"Large\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-E cross-arch std: h0 vs h24-1\",\n            0.45,\n            \"—\",\n            \"Small-Medium\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag cross-arch std: h0 vs h24-1\",\n            0.08,\n            \"—\",\n            \"Negligible\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-008 是 median 档论文的 statistical backbone。核心 message：effect 是 real 且 large on LAMBADA， 但 scope is narrow (only LAMBADA survives correction)，且 robustness to GDN exclusion shows effect sizes shrink substantially (38% vs 79%)。 审稿人会 appreciate 这种 self-critical rigor。GDN-excluded CI lower bound = 22% 意味着即使在 most conservative scenario 下仍有 meaningful convergence，但不是 \\\"dramatic\\\"。 关键写作策略：把 Bonferroni-significant-only-LAMBADA 框架为 \\\"our conservative test confirms the retrieval-gated nature of the effect\\\" 而非 \\\"we failed to find significance elsewhere\\\"。 Effect size table 对 Meta-analysis 友好，审稿人 D 会满意。\\n\\n\\nmedian 档的关键约束是 GDN-excluded 后 effect size 大幅缩水但 directionally survive。 原因：GDN 是三个架构中 convergence 效应最强的（从 aggregate 角度，GDN 在高 attention ratio 时 与其他两个最接近），移除它后跨架构 variance 的基线本身就变小（RetNet 和 HGRN2 的 h0 性能差异 比 GDN 参与时小），导致 std reduction 百分比从 79% 降至 38%。Bootstrap CI 变宽是因为 n=2 architectures 的 pairwise comparison 本质上自由度极低。 但 directional survival 是可信的：RetNet-HGRN2 pair 在 LAMBADA 上确实随 attention 增加而收敛 (ρ=-0.90, p=0.042)，只是 magnitude 更小。 Bonferroni 校正后只有 LAMBADA 存活 (0.008×6=0.048)，这在 median 档下是 expected—— 不改变 \\\"LAMBADA-anchored\\\" 的叙事，反而为 honest scope 提供了 formal justification。 Cohen's d=1.82 (LAMBADA h0 vs h24) 表明 effect size 本身是 large 的；问题不在 \\\"是否存在\\\" 而在 \\\"范围多广\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"对 LAMBADA，将 aggregate convergence curve 与 per-example divergence metrics  (Jaccard, net effect asymmetry) 作为 attention ratio 的函数并列绘制， 展示 convergence 和 divergence 共同演化——attention 越多，aggregate 越收敛但 per-example 越分化。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"convergence_divergence_correlation_rho\": -0.85,\n      \"convergence_divergence_correlation_p\": 0.033,\n      \"convergence_metric\": \"cross-arch std of LAMBADA accuracy\",\n      \"divergence_metric\": \"mean pairwise Jaccard of helped sets (lower = more divergent)\",\n      \"co_evolution_pattern\": \"as attention ratio increases 0→24, cross-arch std decreases monotonically while mean Jaccard also decreases (more architecture-specific effects)\",\n      \"jaccard_at_h0\": 0.15,\n      \"jaccard_at_h3\": 0.1,\n      \"jaccard_at_h6\": 0.08,\n      \"jaccard_at_h12\": 0.07,\n      \"jaccard_at_h24\": 0.06,\n      \"std_at_h0\": 0.024,\n      \"std_at_h3\": 0.015,\n      \"std_at_h6\": 0.01,\n      \"std_at_h12\": 0.007,\n      \"std_at_h24\": 0.005,\n      \"net_effect_asymmetry_gdn_trend\": \"increasingly negative (more hurt) with attention\",\n      \"net_effect_asymmetry_hgrn2_trend\": \"increasingly positive (more helped) with attention\",\n      \"net_effect_asymmetry_retnet_trend\": \"slightly negative, relatively stable\",\n      \"paradox_strength_at_max_attention\": \"strongest — maximum aggregate convergence coexists with minimum per-example overlap\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Convergence-divergence co-evolution across attention ratios (LAMBADA, 1.3B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Attention Ratio\",\n          \"Cross-Arch Std\",\n          \"Mean Pairwise Jaccard (Helped)\",\n          \"GDN Net Effect\",\n          \"HGRN2 Net Effect\",\n          \"RetNet Net Effect\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"h0 (0/12)\",\n            0.024,\n            0.15,\n            0,\n            0,\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"h3-1 (3/12)\",\n            0.015,\n            0.1,\n            -52,\n            48,\n            -18\n          ],\n          [\n            \"h6-1 (6/12)\",\n            0.01,\n            0.08,\n            -98,\n            105,\n            -35\n          ],\n          [\n            \"h12-1 (12/12)\",\n            0.007,\n            0.07,\n            -130,\n            138,\n            -52\n          ],\n          [\n            \"h24-1 (24/24)\",\n            0.005,\n            0.06,\n            -153,\n            153,\n            -69\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"Net Effect = helped_count - hurt_count on LAMBADA. h0 has no attention, so net effects are 0 (baseline). Jaccard at h0 reflects residual overlap from different random initializations.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-010 产出论文最重要的 figure——dual-axis convergence-divergence plot。ρ=-0.85 (p=0.033)  是 median 档论文中最 \\\"clean\\\" 的统计结果之一（仅次于 LAMBADA 的 ρ=-1.0），因为它在单个 benchmark  内利用了 attention ratio 的 5 个梯度点，避免了跨 benchmark dose-response 的 low-n 问题。 这个 figure 同时服务于 Claim 1 (aggregate convergence) 和 Claim 3 (per-example divergence)， 是连接两个 claims 的 bridge evidence。 论文结构建议：在 Results 中先展示 aggregate convergence (Claim 1)，再展示 per-example divergence  (Claim 3)，最后用 exp-010 figure 作为 \\\"synthesis\\\" 展示两者的 co-evolution—— 这就是 \\\"equalizer paradox\\\" 的完整呈现。\\n\\nconvergence-divergence co-evolution 是 equalizer paradox 的核心可视化。在 median 档下， 相关性 ρ=-0.85 (p=0.033) 是显著的——这是 n=5 attention ratios 的 rank correlation， 比跨 benchmark 的 dose-response 有更好的 power（因为这里 both metrics 在同一 benchmark 内变化）。 机制直觉：attention 层越多，每个架构能 \\\"选择性优化\\\" 的样本子集越大，但这些子集由架构内部结构 决定因此互不重叠。GDN 的 delta rule 在高 attention 下更多地 \\\"依赖\\\" attention 来处理精确 retrieval， 但这牺牲了 delta rule 对某些样本的原生优势（hurt 增加）；HGRN2 的 hierarchical gating 与 attention 更互补，所以随 attention 增加变得 increasingly helped。最终 aggregate 收敛是因为三个架构 通过不同路径到达了相似的 accuracy level——但路径本身越来越不同。 Jaccard 从 0.15 (h0) 降至 0.06 (h24) 表明 h0 时 helped/hurt sets 本身就有低重叠 （这可能部分反映 baseline noise），attention 增加后进一步分化。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":647,"startLine":1,"totalLines":647}}}
