{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VfgT5HoE7P7AK2jX41X3pH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the directory exists. Now let me write the complete LaTeX paper.\n\nLet me carefully construct the paper with all the data from the experiment_data.json. I need to be very careful with numbers.\n\nKey data points to include:\n\n**Exp 1: Multi-benchmark per-example analysis**\n- Table with 6 benchmarks: LAMBADA, ARC-Easy, ARC-Challenge, HellaSwag, WinoGrande, MMLU\n- Columns: Benchmark, Retrieval Demand, Aggregate ρ, p, Jaccard, Std Reduction %, Verdict\n\n\n- dose_response_rho_6benchmarks: -0.66, p: 0.16\n\n**Exp 2: Helped/hurt sample characterization Phase 2**\n- Perplexity and topic features showing GDN perplexity with p=0.031 and d=0.19, while topic features remain non-significant\n- Cross-architecture interaction at p=0.07\n\n**Exp 3: Attention weight extraction**\n- Analyzing attention entropy, target context focus, and their correlation with helped/hurt outcomes across architectures\n\n**Exp 4: Architecture expansion**\n- Final set of 3 architectures, no additional ones identified\n\n**Exp 5: 340M rebound**\n- Characterizing rebound samples with 62% overlap in the hardest 20%, though training tokens show correlation (r=0.31) that hasn't been fully disentangled\n\n**Exp 6: Statistical robustness**\n- Bootstrap confidence intervals show LAMBADA achieves 77% [68%, 84%] standard deviation reduction while GDN-excluded drops to 38% [22%, 53%], with only LAMBADA surviving Bonferroni correction at p=0.048\n- Effect sizes are substantial: LAMBADA shows Cohen's d of 1.82 between h0 and h24 compared to ARC-E's 0.45, with η² = 0.71\n\n**Exp 7: Convergence-divergence bridge**\n- Strong negative correlation (ρ = -0.85, p = 0.033) with Jaccard similarity declining from 0.15 to 0.06 and standard deviation dropping from 0.024 to 0.005, while GDN becomes increasingly negative and HGRN2 increasingly posit